{"segs": ["PA_ja_114:0.1"], "en": "Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_114:0.2", "PA_ja_114:0.3"], "en": "Ekakanipāta, Haṃsivagga (The Section on the Swan)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_114:0.4"], "en": "4. The Jātaka of Mitacinti:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_114:1.1", "PA_ja_114:1.2"], "en": "“The one who thinks much and the one who thinks little—both were caught in the net.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_114:1.3"], "en": "“Mitacintī brought about their release;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_114:1.4"], "en": "there, both were reunited.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_114:2.1"], "en": "Thus ends the fourth Jātaka, the Mitacintī-jātaka.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
]
